lation 'divides'",review:{status:"unverified",drafted:"ai",date:"2026-08-21",note:"flagged retroactively; record authored earlier under the pre-review-field workflow"}},{id:"bar-angle-angle-bar",tex:"\\left| a \\right\\rangle \\left\\langle b \\right|",description:"ket followed by bra: |a><b| outer product / projector",concepts:["ketbra"],mathcatBehaviour:"absent \u2014 no inference; symbols spoken",priority:"high for physics/QC \u2014 equal labels = projector; physics \\ketbra \\outerproduct \\dyad \\op all produce it; starred variants emit a FLAT token run (no wrapper mrow, non-stretchy bars)",review:{status:"unverified",drafted:"ai",date:"2026-08-21",note:"flagged retroactively; record authored earlier under the pre-review-field workflow"}},{id:"angle-bar-bar-angle",tex:"\\left\\langle m | A | n \\right\\rangle",description:"angle brackets with two internal vertical bars: matrix-element sandwich",concepts:["matrix-element","expectation-value"],mathcatBehaviour:"absent \u2014 SRE reads both bars as 'divides'; starred physics variants misread as absolute value",priority:"high for physics \u2014 <psi|A|psi> with equal labels is the expectation-value reading (author chooses); physics \\mel \\matrixelement and 2-arg \\expval produce it",review:{status:"unverified",drafted:"ai",date:"2026-08-21",note:"flagged retroactively; record authored earlier under the pre-review-field workflow"}},{id:"bar-angle",tex:"\\left| \\psi \\right\\rangle",description:"vertical bar opening, right angle bracket closing: a standalone ket",concepts:["ket"],mathcatBehaviour:"absent \u2014 no bra-ket inference (inferred from the angle-bar-angle family probing; standalone shape not separately probed)",priority:"high for physics/QC \u2014 asymmetric delimiters defeat symmetric pairing; SRE reads it 'divides psi right angle bracket' (probed 2026-08-20, gen-review-sheet harness)",review:{status:"unverified",drafted:"ai",date:"2026-08-20"}},{id:"angle-bar",tex:"\\left\\langle \\psi \\right|",description:"left angle bracket opening, vertical bar closing: a standalone bra",concepts:["bra"],mathcatBehaviour:"absent \u2014 no bra-ket inference (inferred from the angle-bar-angle family probing; standalone shape not separately probed)",priority:"high for physics/QC \u2014 same asymmetry as bar-angle; SRE reads it 'left angle bracket psi divides' (probed 2026-08-20); frequently carries a trailing subscript (\\langle z|_{A})",review:{status:"unverified",drafted:"ai",date:"2026-08-20"}},{id:"bracket-bar",tex:"\\left[ A | b \\right]",description:"square brackets with an internal vertical bar",concepts:["augmented-matrix","conditional-expectation"],mathcatBehaviour:"unknown \u2014 not probed; bar likely read as 'divides' (inferred from the vertical-bar family; probe pending)",priority:"high for linear algebra \u2014 50/50 of Math_22a's bracket-bar hits are augmented matrices; genuinely two-reading with E[X|Y] conditional expectation (probability), so both concepts are offered",review:{status:"unverified",drafted:"ai",date:"2026-08-21",note:"spoken form for augmented-matrix sweep-informed 2026-08-20 ('A augmented with b', attested verb form; see concept notes + PRECISION-REVIEW \xA710) but still needs instructor word-for-word confirmation; revisit after the table-properties review"}},{id:"bar-relation",tex:"a \\mid b",description:"a vertical bar as a binary relation between operands: divisibility (a|b, a \\mid b) and its negation (a \\nmid b, a \\not| b)",concepts:["divisible-by","not-divisible-by"],mathcatBehaviour:"SRE PROBED 2026-08-20 (test/probe-mid-speech.mjs): clearspeak default is already 'a divides b' for \\mid (U+2223), \\nmid (U+2224 -> 'a does not divide b'), AND bare | (U+7C); mathspeak stays syntactic 'vertical bar' except \\nmid -> 'does not divide'. MathCAT default for U+2223 is documented 'divides' (NSoiffer/MathCAT#212) \u2014 local browser probe still pending. VERBALIZATION SWEEP 2026-08-20 (PRECISION-REVIEW \xA710): 'a divides b' is the PRIMARY formal